Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 16:40:38 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] P15C Wave 2 (c): the 2040 freeze is the tick's last step
 (1361-E3 r1)

1359-A section 4 and section 10 item 6, commit (c), with 1361-F
ruling 9:
- src/core/campaignLegacy.ts: freezeCampaignLegacyWeek(state). In the
  tick producing week 6240, when the industry and the root both record
  from before 6240 and no official manifest exists, it builds the facts
  of the tick's final state, calls the law through freezeLegacy, stamps
  campaign-legacy-<n> with the p15c.finale triple, and advances
  p15Sequence. Every other tick returns its input unchanged. No
  randomness, no clock.
- validateCampaignLegacy gains the marker rule's other half: a save that
  stands at or past 6240 with the freeze due must hold the official
  manifest (1359-A section 4.3).
- tick.ts: the freeze wraps the Power Ranking record, which wraps
  everything before it, so it is the tick's last step and the official
  sequence is the week's last allocation; P15A.1's step 2.5 is untouched.

A save below 6240 freezes on its 6240 tick, with migrated siblings read
as limited; a save at or past 6240 never freezes (1359-A section 5.2).
On this base the market domain reads notRecorded at 2040, because (b)'s
tick write keeps sharedMarket recording from the current week (1361-F5
ruling 2.3).

